  "description": "PROCESS-ENTER-KEY's FIRST arm at app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl:146-151, which no other case in this folder reaches: USRIDINI is blank, so 'User ID can NOT be empty...' is issued, the cursor is put back on USRIDINL and the screen is sent once. The two IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON blocks at :157 and :166 are both skipped, so USRSEC is never opened - the expectedWrites list is empty and the final state is the seeded state, which is a positive assertion that no repository call happened rather than an absence of interest.\n\nThe blank is expressed as LOW-VALUES (X'00'), not spaces. The condition is written 'WHEN USRIDINI = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES', so both figurative constants take the same arm, and a translation that tested only for spaces - or that trimmed the field before testing it - would pass every spaces-based case and fail here. case13 drives the same kind of guard with spaces, so the pair covers both figurative constants.",
